Record the seed each panel and each estimator actually used (M8).
=================================================================

Applies ON TOP of theta-mutation.patch, in the disposable clone only:

    cd /home/user/donor-smoke
    git apply .../theta-mutation.patch
    git apply .../m8-seed-log.patch

This is a diff, not vendored source (D5: the donor has no licence).

WHY
---
The M8 design rests on one structural sentence: "nine new truths attach to
the same clusters without disturbing what is there." F13-F16 are all cases of
a structural sentence that was true-sounding and unchecked, so this one gets
evidence from the run rather than from the source that asserts it -- F11's
lesson, where two-lane isolation was asserted and only an empty library
exposed it.

WHAT IT ADDS
------------
0. generate_panels.R writes metadata.json with `digits = NA`. jsonlite's
   DEFAULT is digits = 4, and run_tools.py:445 reads effect_pct from exactly
   that file -- so theta = -0.03125 was recorded as -0.0312, moving a
   preregistered decision-boundary truth off the boundary it exists to sit
   on. The donor never hit it (0 and 0.075 are 4-dp exact); the
   theta-mutation patch introduced values that are not. Same mechanism as
   D12, whose own remedy line already read "one argument, digits = NA" --
   applied there to the tool-output path and not to this one. See F17.

1. generate_panels.R writes results/raw/panel_seeds.csv, one row per panel:
       scenario, effect_label, iteration, effect_pct, panel_seed, noise_seed
   The checkable property is that panel_seed is CONSTANT across effect_label
   within (scenario, iteration). That is what makes the arms a
   common-random-numbers design; mistaking it for independence is F16.

   The write sits immediately after the generation loop and BEFORE the figure
   section, so a plotting failure cannot lose the evidence.

2. run_tools.py records estimator_seed on every emitted row:
       causalpy      iteration   (run_causalpy.py sets random_seed=iteration)
       causalimpact  iteration   (run_tools.py passes --seed iteration)
       geolift       None        (takes no seed; deterministic given the panel)
       google_mm     None        (takes no seed; deterministic given the panel)
   Both seeded paths are guarded by `if iteration is not None`, so recording
   `iteration` records exactly what was passed.

VERIFIED, not illustrative
--------------------------
    Rscript parse()     generate_panels.R parses, 57 expressions
    py_compile          run_tools.py compiles
    live run            360 seed records written; panel_seed constant across
                        all 9 effect labels in all 40 clusters; every seed
                        equal to 42000 + 10000*scenario_idx + iteration
    metadata precision  {"eff_m031": -0.03125, "eff_p052": 0.051875,
                        "eff_p104": 0.104375} -- exact after the fix,
                        -0.0312 / 0.0519 / 0.1044 before it
    labels              no collision with the existing seven truths

WHAT IT DOES NOT CHANGE
-----------------------
No estimator input, no RNG, no estimate. It adds one CSV, one JSON field,
and precision to a field that was already there. The pilot was re-run from
scratch after the precision fix and the first run kept as a baseline, so
"metadata precision does not touch estimation" is measured rather than
assumed -- see m8_pilot_check.py section 7.

